    "result_text": "All 65 tests pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the immutable structured `OWNER_CREATED` audit event. The acceptance test `Cp53Tests` was already present (and failing); it's now green, along with the full suite (65 tests, 0 failures).\n\n**What I added:**\n\n1. **`OwnerEventSequence`** (`rest/support/`) \u2014 a `@Component` singleton wrapping an `AtomicLong`, handing out a strictly increasing `seq` via `next()`. Being a process-wide bean, sequence numbers increase monotonically across creates regardless of request thread.\n\n2. **`OwnerCreatedEvent`** (`rest/function/owner/`) \u2014 an immutable `record` capturing `seq`, `ownerId`, the owner's primary identifier, and `membershipLevel` at construction. It serializes to the specified JSON `{seq, ownerId, customerCode, membershipLevel, event:'OWNER_CREATED'}`. Crucially, the identifier flows through a **single point** \u2014 the `from(seq, owner)` factory reads `owner.getCustomerCode()` and one `IDENTIFIER_FIELD` constant names the JSON key. When the customerCode is later unified into the memberId, only those two spots change and the event automatically carries the memberId, exactly as the spec requires.\n\n3. **`EmitOwnerCreatedEvent`** (`rest/function/owner/`) \u2014 an OfficeFloor function step that draws the next `seq`, builds the event, and logs its JSON to the `AUDIT` logger (in addition to the existing human-readable audit line). `membershipLevel` is computed via `Membership.levelOf(owner)`, matching `AuditOwnerCreated` for consistency.\n\n4. Wired a new `emitEvent` step into `owners.POST.yml` right after `audit` (so the owner id already exists), under the same `transaction` governance as the rest of the pipeline.\n\nObserved output confirms both lines emit:\n```\nAUDIT - owner created id=11 customerCode=NSW-16E6609E ...\nAUDIT - {\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"customerCode\":\"NSW-16E6609E\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}\n```",
